"""Shared creative rule for new designs, full refreshes and targeted artwork edits."""

SIGNATURE_FREE_COMPOSITION = """SIGNATURE-FREE COLLECTOR COMPOSITION

Do not search for, source, generate, trace, reproduce or include athlete signatures or autographs. Do not replace them with invented signatures, digitally illustrated autographs or handwriting-style athlete names.

Create the premium limited-edition collector feel through the existing title hierarchy, refined typography, balanced composition, intentional negative space and the official Sports Cave edition badge.

Treat the subject, title, name, supporting context and edition badge as one coordinated composition. Refine their scale, alignment, line spacing and separation so every element feels deliberately placed and remains readable at thumbnail size and intended print size.

Do not reserve an empty “signature slot.” Use the available space by thoughtfully arranging the existing elements. Where beneficial, reposition the official edition badge in relation to the typography, keeping it subordinate to the subject and title, comfortably separated from neighbouring elements, and inside the established safe area. Preserve the exact official badge asset and edition number.

Do not automatically fill space with additional wording, repeated names, statistics, quotes, oversized numbers, extra portraits, decorative symbols or substitute seals. Add supporting context only when it strengthens the sporting story and meets the existing verification requirements. Leave breathing room where it improves the design.

Choose placement for each artwork individually. Do not force a fixed title-and-badge arrangement across every design.

For new designs and full refreshes, apply this rule throughout the composition. For targeted edits to approved artwork, remove an existing signature only when requested, then adjust only the spacing and nearby typography or badge placement needed to restore balance. Preserve all other approved elements.

Final check: no autograph or simulated signing; clear typography hierarchy; balanced visual weight; readable collector details; comfortable spacing; intact borders and safe areas. The artwork should feel complete and collectible without a signature.

All existing source checks, subject-authenticity protections, master-canvas requirements, official badge rules, production specifications and delivery steps remain in force."""
